## Bug found and fixed
The coverage pass found a bug in the sorted store scans. `SortedMapStore` and `SortedSetStore` built two of the scan bounds by adding `~` to an encoded rank:
- **Exclusive start:** used `` `${rank}~` ``.
- **Inclusive end:** also used `` `${rank}~` ``.

But `~` (0x7E) is not the next rank after an arbitrary rank. I confirmed with `makeEncodePassable` that `'sbetaa' < 'sbeta~'`. So:
- an exclusive start of `'beta'` silently dropped `'betaa'`;
- an inclusive end of `'gamma'` wrongly included `'gammaa'`.

The existing tests didn't catch it because none of their keys had another key as a prefix.

